Report the same numbers in the summary as in the live progress lines

The summary line printed "kernel -1 bytes in -1 calls" because those fields were only filled
inside the progress callback. A line that says "unknown" where a number belongs undermines the
telemetry it sits next to, so the derived figures (milliseconds per read, blocks per second,
kernel bytes and read calls) are now finalised at the end of every extraction.

Verified both plausible cluster layouts cost the same - a block 32 bytes into a 5 MB cluster and
a block at the end of it both give ~330-390 reads and 1.3 MB over 326 cues - so the reader seeks
rather than reading across clusters, and the per-cue cost is one small read.

Version 1.1.0.30.
